# What `gcloud run deploy --source swadharmaservices.in` uploads to Cloud Build.
#
# This is NOT the same question as what the Dockerfile COPYs. Without this file
# gcloud uploads the whole directory to a Cloud Build source bucket, and this
# directory holds things that must not go there:
#
#   Edu/          student rosters — personal data. The repository already
#                 refuses them (.gitignore, "keep student rosters out of the
#                 repository"); a GCS build bucket is no better a home.
#   _layout/      the page sources, plus build_pages.py and relink_legacy.py
#   *.md          DEPLOY_RUNBOOK, ONBOARDING_API, PROFESSIONAL_ENROLMENT_API —
#                 internal notes and API contracts
#   test_*.py     the test suites
#   .claude/      session logs
#
# So this is an allowlist, not a denylist: everything is excluded, then the five
# things the image actually needs are added back. A file dropped into this
# folder later is excluded by default rather than uploaded by default, which is
# the safer way round for a directory that has held personal data.

*

!Dockerfile
!nginx.conf
!*.html
!*.css
!*.js

# panchanga.json by name, deliberately NOT !*.json. It is the only JSON the site
# serves, and this workspace has Firebase service-account keys sitting in
# neighbouring folders — a blanket !*.json would let one reach a build context
# the moment somebody copied it in. Named files cannot do that.
!panchanga.json
